$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Grubbs catalyst first generation (2.1 mg, 2.5 μmol, 10 mol %) was added
to a solution of acrylate 34 (13.0 mg, 25 μmol, 1 equiv) in dry CH2Cl2 (5
mL) at 40 °C. After 4 h, the solvent was removed in vacuo, and the
residue was subjected to flash chromatography (SiO2, hexanes:EtOAc, 90:10
to 75:25). The dihydropyranone 35 (10.8 mg, 22 μmol) as a brownish oil in
88% yield. The product was considered pure and was immediately used in
next step.
